+{"id":"CF-093","title":"P4 - README Status rows 1 and 3 are enforced by nothing: strip the interpreter-qualified --check command from both and the whole suite still prints SELFTEST: PASS (exit 0)","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T17:38:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T17:38:42Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"a96c5ee33c4837774ee289d0342255704c428097e1857894902ee6a809770270","fingerprint_algo":"sha256 of the row's probe string as published (jq -r '.[0].probe' <draft> | sha256sum)","lane":"readme-qa","tick":"code-factory-readme-qa-2026-11-03-16-51-21","measured_at":"2026-11-03T17:40:00Z","measured_commit":"d107ac40965eabac139ed60f9f5b474f7df63ba2"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 at origin/main d107ac4 (canonical checkout, clean tracked tree, parity 0/0) by the readme-qa tick. CF-064 and CF-092 were both closed by editing README prose: row 3 and row 1 now name `HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3.12 scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check`. Both closures reproduce on re-run at d107ac4: docs/audits/cf092-install-check-arms.txt regenerates from docs/audits/cf092-arms.sh with identical arm bodies (1 vs 4 gate rows, 0/1 gate rows naming binary and port, exit 1 on both arms), and `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS. What neither closure tested is whether anything can fail when that prose regresses. Measured: replacing the qualified form with the unqualified command in BOTH README rows leaves the full suite printing `SELFTEST: PASS` with exit 0. The only arms that read README.md are arm 9 (every prompts/*.md named by the README exists) and arm 15 (CF-054's project-node re-run line); nothing binds Status rows 1 or 3, so the same early-gate class CF-064 and CF-092 fixed can return silently on the next README edit. The only artifact that would catch it is the arms transcript, whose regeneration is manual and unenforced. Repo precedent cuts both ways: CF-054 shipped a selftest arm for the row it fixed and CF-085 shipped tests/test_lane_target.py for its guard, while the two interpreter rows were closed doc-only. Distinct from CF-064 and CF-092 (both acceptance criteria hold and reproduce), and distinct from CF-081 (hand-typed docs/BOARD.md state) and CF-090 (tree-wide ruff-format lint): this row is the missing enforcement, not the text.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree: the row's probe prints `qualified_command_occurrences=0`, `SELFTEST: PASS`, `SELFTEST_EXIT=0` and leaves README.md byte-identical.\n1. `bash tests/selftest.sh` gains an arm that binds README Status rows 1 and 3 to the interpreter-qualified form: it FAILS when either row's re-run cell offers only `scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check` without `HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3.12`.\n2. The arm carries a negative fixture that proves it can fail: in one run it prints a FAIL row naming the regressed row for a mutated README copy with the qualified form stripped, and a PASS row for the shipped README.\n3. At the fixed tip `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS (exit 0) and the same probe prints `SELFTEST_EXIT=1`, i.e. the probe flips from green to red once the fix lands, proving the new arm is the thing that fails.\n4. `scripts/boardctl validate` prints RESULT: OK at the fixed tip.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); cp README.md \"$d/orig\"; trap 'cp \"$d/orig\" README.md' EXIT; sed -i 's#HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3\\.12 scripts/harness/install-hermes\\.sh --check#scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check#g' README.md; echo \"qualified_command_occurrences=$(grep -c 'HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3.12 scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check' README.md)\"; bash tests/selftest.sh > \"$d/out\" 2>&1; rc=$?; tail -1 \"$d/out\"; echo \"SELFTEST_EXIT=$rc\""}
